#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When a chemist runs an NMR experiment, they place a sample of nuclear spins "
"in a strong magnetic field, apply a radio-frequency (RF) pulse, and measure "
"the signal that comes back. The technique rests on a few ideas from the "
"quantum mechanics of a spin-1/2 particle in a magnetic field. The spin has "
"two energy levels separated by an energy that corresponds to a "
"characteristic Larmor frequency. A resonant pulse at that frequency tips the"
" spin into the transverse plane, where it precesses and induces a signal "
"that then fades with two characteristic times, $T_1$ and $T_2$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A superconducting **qubit** is an engineered version of the same object: a "
"controllable two-level quantum system. Its $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ "
"states are the analog of spin-up and spin-down, the gate we apply to rotate "
"it is the analog of the RF pulse, and it loses coherence with its own $T_1$ "
"and $T_2$. This is not merely a loose comparison; some of the earliest "
"experimental quantum processors in the late 1990s and early 2000s used "
"NMR.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this module you will use a real quantum computer to run the same "
"characterization experiments that an NMR spectroscopist (or a quantum "
"engineer calibrating hardware) performs:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Rabi / nutation** — driving the spin and watching it rotate. This is how "
"you calibrate a $\\pi$ or $\\pi/2$ rotation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$T_1$** — spin-lattice relaxation, the decay of an excited spin back to "
"equilibrium.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$T_2$** — spin-spin relaxation (dephasing), measured with a Ramsey "
"experiment and refocused with a Hahn echo.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**NMR spectroscopy (chemical shift and $J$-coupling)** — simulating a small "
"molecule on several qubits and reading its multiplet spectrum to recover "
"connectivity through the $n+1$ rule.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each concept we first give the minimal theory, then implement the "
"experiment in Qiskit following the four-step *Qiskit patterns* workflow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Spin-1/2 particles in a magnetic field {#spin-12-particles-in-a-magnetic-"
"field}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A spin-1/2 nucleus has a magnetic moment $\\boldsymbol{\\mu} = \\gamma "
"\\hbar \\mathbf{I}$, where $\\gamma$ is the gyromagnetic ratio. In a static "
"field $B_0$ along $z$, the two spin states split in energy (the **Zeeman "
"effect**):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$E_{\\pm} = \\mp \\tfrac{1}{2}\\gamma \\hbar B_0, \\qquad \\Delta E = "
"\\gamma \\hbar B_0 = \\hbar \\omega_0 .$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The energy gap defines the **Larmor (resonance) frequency** $\\omega_0 = "
"\\gamma B_0$. The magnetic moment **precesses** about $B_0$ at this same "
"frequency.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To rotate the spin we apply an oscillating RF field at (or near) "
"$\\omega_0$. In the frame rotating at the drive frequency (the **rotating "
"frame**), a resonant drive rotates the Bloch vector about an axis in the "
"$x$-$y$ plane. How far it rotates (the **flip angle**) is set by the pulse's"
" strength and duration. Two choices matter most: a $90^\\circ$ pulse tips a "
"$+1/2$ spin into the transverse plane, and a $180^\\circ$ pulse rotates it "
"fully to $-1/2$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Translating between NMR and quantum computing jargon {#translating-between-"
"nmr-and-quantum-computing-jargon}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A qubit is a two-level system, mathematically identical to a spin-1/2 in a "
"magnetic field &mdash; so while we're running on a quantum processor rather "
"than a nucleus, the physics is the same physics that underlies NMR. Only the"
" vocabulary differs. This table helps you talk to physical chemists and "
"quantum-computing specialists alike.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| NMR / spin-1/2 | Quantum processor (qubit) |\n"
"| ---|---|\n"
"| Spin-up / spin-down | $\\ket{0}$ / $\\ket{1}$ |\n"
"| Zeeman gap $\\Delta E = \\hbar\\omega_0$ | Qubit transition energy $\\hbar\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Larmor frequency $\\omega_0$ | Qubit frequency $\\omega_{01}$ |\n"
"| Resonant RF pulse (flip angle $\\theta$) | Single-qubit rotation gate $R_X(\\theta)$ |\n"
"| $90^\\circ$ / $180^\\circ$ pulse | $R_X(\\pi/2)$ / $R_X(\\pi)$ |\n"
"| Spin-lattice relaxation $T_1$ | Qubit energy-relaxation time $T_1$ |\n"
"| Spin-spin relaxation $T_2$ | Qubit dephasing time $T_2$ |\n"
"| Nutation | Rabi oscillations |\n"
"| Free induction decay (FID), Hahn echo | Ramsey, echo sequences |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Everything below is an exercise in measuring the right-hand column and "
"reading it as the left-hand column.\n"
msgstr ""

