#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Experiment: Rabi oscillations (nutation) {#experiment-rabi-oscillations-"
"nutation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theory {#theory-1}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Drive a spin on resonance and its Bloch vector rotates steadily from pole to"
" pole &mdash; it **nutates**. If we apply a rotation of flip angle $\\theta$"
" about the $x$-axis to a qubit starting in $|0\\rangle$, the probability of "
"finding it in $|1\\rangle$ is:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$P_1(\\theta) = \\sin^2\\!\\left(\\tfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = "
"\\tfrac{1}{2}\\bigl(1 - \\cos\\theta\\bigr).$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the **Rabi curve**. Its first maximum is the $\\pi$ pulse (full "
"inversion, the $180^\\circ$ pulse); a $\\pi/2$ pulse is a quarter-turn (the "
"$90^\\circ$ pulse that tips a spin into the transverse plane). In NMR this "
"curve is how you *calibrate* your pulses.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Experimental caveat\">\n"
"A *literal* Rabi experiment sweeps the drive amplitude or duration in time. That requires pulse-level control, which was removed in Qiskit v2.0. Here we instead sweep the **rotation angle** $\\theta$ of an $R_X(\\theta)$ gate. The curve and the $\\pi$/$\\pi/2$ identification are identical; the only difference is that we choose an angle directly instead of calibrating a pulse length. On hardware with *fractional gates*, $R_X(\\theta)$ for arbitrary $\\theta$ runs natively.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A Bloch-sphere view {#a-bloch-sphere-view}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The animation below shows the **nutation**: a resonant drive rotates the "
"Bloch vector steadily about the $x$-axis, carrying it from $|0\\rangle$ down"
" toward $|1\\rangle$ and back. This is the very motion the Rabi curve "
"measures.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<IBMVideo id=\"135063678\" title=\"Bloch-sphere animation of Rabi nutation "
"about the x-axis.\"/>\n"
msgstr ""

